This product includes work derived from openai/codex-security, also licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The method — threat-model first, fan out to find candidates, verify each one,
render the report deterministically — is theirs. So, kept close to verbatim in
spirit and in several cases in wording, are:

  * the severity policy's distinction between impact, likelihood and the
    additional criteria a critical must satisfy;
  * the counterevidence checklist, and the named list of invalid rebuttals;
  * the instance-splitting rules that keep sibling findings from collapsing
    into a single row.

Where opensec diverges — computed severity with no `ignore` value, coverage
derived from traces rather than self-report, a single four-verb write tool, and
per-phase model routing — it diverges deliberately, and those choices are ours
to defend.
